    "body": "## Purpose\n\nPart of #59055 (sleep-mode memory). Same pattern as #62358 (LoRA).\n\nAttention backend impls derive device tensors from their inputs/weights, e.g. ALiBi slopes (built in `__init__`) and the FlashInfer/B12x fp32 sinks copy (built in `process_weights_after_loading`). With `enable_sleep_mode`, model construction runs inside the `weights` cuMem pool, so these tensors land there too. Level-2 sleep discards that pool, and they are not parameters or buffers, so nothing restores them: after wake-up the model generates garbage even though the weights are correct.\n\nThis PR builds the impl, and runs the impl's `process_weights_after_loading`, inside the `runtime` pool when sleep mode is on. Sleep offloads and restores the `runtime` pool at every level, so the impl state survives. No backend changes; nothing changes without sleep mode or on non-CUDA-alike platforms.\n\nSplit out of #60009.\n\n## Test Plan\n\n`sleep_ab.py`: greedy baseline, then 3 x (sleep(level=2) -> wake -> regenerate, compare tokens), GSM8K before/after. `inplace` = `sleep_preserve_parameter_names=[\"*\"]`; `reload` = wake weights, `reload_weights()`, wake KV cache. GB200.\n\n## Test Result\n\nPrompts with tokens identical to the pre-sleep greedy baseline, per cycle (3 cycles):\n\n| Config | Mode | main | this PR |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| bloom-560m ALiBi, Triton attention | inplace | 0/8 x3 | 8/8 x3 |\n| bloom-560m ALiBi, Triton attention | reload | 0/8 x3 | 8/8 x3 |\n| bloom-560m ALiBi, FlashAttention | inplace | 0/8 x3 | 8/8 x3 |\n| bloom-560m ALiBi, FlashAttention | reload | 0/8 x3 | 8/8 x3 |\n| gpt-oss-20b sinks, FlashInfer attention, Marlin MXFP4 MoE | inplace | 0/8 x3 (GSM8K .31 -> .12) | 8/8 x3 (GSM8K .32 -> .33) |\n| gpt-oss-20b sinks, FlashInfer attention, Marlin MXFP4 MoE | reload | 0/8 x3 | 0/8 x3 |\n\nThe gpt-oss reload row fails the same way on main and here; it comes from the Marlin MXFP4 MoE reload path, not attention (separate issue).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
